[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Flight-dynamics checks high-level requirements
UID: FMD-HLR-DYN
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Behaviour of the four flight-dynamics checks as built: rate-loop oscillation, vibration, estimator (EKF) health
and the ascent profile. Code: `flightmd_core/analysers/oscillation.py`, `vibration.py`, `ekf.py` and
`ascent_profile.py`. Each check takes the topic tables and the parameter set of one log and returns one
`AnalyserResult`. Low-level requirements are in `llr-dyn.sdoc`; the design is in `06-design/lld-dyn.md`.
All times are log-relative microseconds on input; findings carry milliseconds and seconds.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Oscillation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oscillation inputs and not assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
The oscillation check shall take the topic `vehicle_angular_velocity` (a `timestamp` column and roll, pitch and
yaw rate in rad/s). It shall return a not-assessed result with a reason, and no score, when the topic is absent,
when it has no `timestamp` column, when no axis is logged at 10 Hz or more in flight, or when no in-flight
stretch without a gap is long enough for one analysis window of about 4 s.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oscillation found per window, in flight
STATEMENT: >>>
The oscillation check shall use in-air samples only, shall look for the largest narrow spectral peak in
overlapping windows of about 4 s between 1 Hz and the lower of 100 Hz and 0.4 times the sample rate, and shall
report its frequency in Hz, its amplitude in deg/s and the time span over which it is present, so that a short
burst in a long log is found and the amplitude does not depend on the length of the log.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover burst detection, time span, frequency and amplitude. No test in `tests/test_oscillation.py` supplies
arming data, so the in-air restriction is checked by inspection of `OscillationAnalyser.analyse`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oscillation severity and module score
STATEMENT: >>>
For each axis the oscillation check shall raise at most one finding: info at an amplitude of 5 deg/s or more,
warning at 15 deg/s or more and critical at 40 deg/s or more, and only when the peak is at least 25 times the
median power in the band, both taken as the median of three neighbouring windows. The module score shall be 100
less 5, 15 or 30 for each axis with an info, warning or critical finding, not below 0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: What an oscillation finding and result carry
STATEMENT: >>>
An oscillation finding shall carry the category `oscillation`, a `kind` of `oscillation.rate_p`,
`oscillation.rate_d` or `oscillation.mechanical`, the axis and frequency in its title, the measured amplitude,
threshold, prominence and duration in its text, the time window when one is known, a confidence from 0 to 1 and
the spectrum for a chart. The result shall carry, for every assessed axis and whether or not a finding fired,
the peak frequency, the prominence and the amplitude as key metrics.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oscillation advice by band and vehicle
STATEMENT: >>>
The oscillation check shall attribute a peak below 12 Hz to the rate P gain, a peak from 12 Hz to below 35 Hz to
the rate D gain or D-term filtering, and a peak at 35 Hz or above to a mechanical cause with no gain change. It
shall name the P or D gain of the autopilot and frame type found in the parameter set (PX4 or ArduPilot,
multirotor or fixed wing) and shall give a numeric change only when that gain is in the log with a value above
zero: the P gain times 0.87, or the D gain times 0.85. It shall give no numeric change for a VTOL, a rover, an
unknown vehicle, ArduPilot fixed-wing yaw or a PX4 fixed-wing D gain.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the P band for PX4 multirotor, PX4 fixed wing, ArduPilot multirotor, rover and an unknown vehicle,
and the D band for PX4 multirotor. The mechanical band, VTOL, ArduPilot fixed wing and the D-band filter names
are checked by inspection of `_finding` and of `RATE_GAINS` in `vehicle.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-006
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Recommended gain held inside the firmware range
STATEMENT: >>>
The oscillation check shall hold a recommended gain value inside the firmware metadata range for that parameter,
or withhold it with a note, and shall not recommend a value equal to the current value or equal to zero.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Not built. As built the value is the current value times 0.87 or 0.85, rounded to 4 or 5 decimal places, with no
lower bound (LLR-DYN-014, LLR-DYN-015).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-016

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Vibration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Vibration sources and not assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
The vibration check shall take its level from the first of these that gives enough in-flight samples: the PX4
`vehicle_imu_status` vibration metric (10 samples), the autopilot `vibration` topic (10 samples), raw
`sensor_accel` (50 samples), each for every logged IMU instance. It shall return a not-assessed result with a
reason when none of the three topics is present or none gives enough in-flight samples.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the priority of the PX4 metric over raw data and the absent-topic case. No test drives the
not-enough-samples skip; it is checked by inspection of `VibrationAnalyser.analyse`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Vibration limits per source
STATEMENT: >>>
The vibration check shall raise a warning when an IMU's level is above the first limit and a critical finding
when it is above the second: 4.905 and 9.81 m/s2 for the PX4 accelerometer vibration metric (also when a PX4
vehicle reports it as `vibration_z`), 30 and 60 m/s2 for the `vibration` topic of any other vehicle and for the
level computed from raw accelerometer data. The level shall be the 95th percentile of the in-flight samples for
the autopilot's own metrics and the whole-flight RMS of the three axes after removing content below about 5 Hz
for raw data.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Vibration counted in flight only
STATEMENT: >>>
The vibration check shall count levels, clipping and sensor errors from in-air samples only, and shall treat the
whole log as flight when the log carries no arming data.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Accelerometer clipping
STATEMENT: >>>
The vibration check shall report accelerometer clipping in flight per IMU, from the autopilot's clip counters
where logged (info for 1 to 99 clips, warning for 100 or more) and otherwise from raw samples that sit flat at a
range limit of 75 m/s2 or more (warning when at least 10 samples and at least 0.1 % of the in-flight samples).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: IMU disagreement and sensor errors
STATEMENT: >>>
The vibration check shall raise a warning when the levels of two or more IMU instances differ by more than half
the warning limit of the source in use, and an info finding for an IMU whose driver error counters rose by 10 or
more in flight.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Vibration score and what the result carries
STATEMENT: >>>
The vibration module score shall be 100 less 30 for each critical and 15 for each warning level finding, 5 for
each sensor-error finding, 15 or 5 for each warning or info clipping finding and 15 for an IMU disagreement, not
below 0. Every finding shall carry the category `vibration`, a `kind`, a confidence from 0 to 1 and chart data.
The result shall carry the worst level as a fraction of its warning limit, the total clip count and the highest
level as key metrics.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Estimator (EKF) health

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EKF inputs, armed time and not assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
The EKF check shall take any of `estimator_status`, `estimator_innovation_test_ratios` and `ekf_test_ratios`,
shall use samples from armed time only (with no arming data: from the first sample with a valid attitude
solution), and shall return a not-assessed result with a reason when none of the topics is present or none has
two or more armed samples.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the armed-time restriction, the no-arming-data rule and the absent-topic case. No test drives the
fewer-than-two-samples skip; it is checked by inspection of `EKFAnalyser.analyse`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Innovation rejections and test ratios
STATEMENT: >>>
The EKF check shall report each innovation check the estimator failed (PX4 `innovation_check_flags` bits 0 to
12) and each innovation test ratio above 1.0, as a warning when the longest run lasts 0.5 s or more and as info
otherwise. It shall report as a warning a test ratio that never exceeds 1.0 and stays above 0.64 for 2.0 s or
more. All ratios are read on one scale on which 1.0 means the measurement was rejected.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Solution validity, GPS glitch and accelerometer error
STATEMENT: >>>
The EKF check shall raise a warning for each solution estimate (attitude, absolute vertical position, and once
first valid: horizontal and vertical velocity, relative and absolute horizontal position) that is invalid for 1 %
or more of the armed samples, a warning when the estimator's GPS-glitch flag is set in any armed sample, and a
critical finding when a PX4 estimator's bad-accelerometer flag is set in any armed sample. The GPS-glitch bit
shall be chosen by source: bit 10 for PX4, bit 14 for an ArduPilot dataflash log, bit 15 for an ArduPilot
telemetry log.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ArduPilot filter faults and measurement timeouts
STATEMENT: >>>
From `ekf_test_ratios` the EKF check shall report each ArduPilot filter fault bit (0 to 7) set in any armed
sample, critical for a NaN attitude or velocity estimate and warning otherwise, and shall raise a warning for a
position, velocity, height or magnetometer timeout that lasts 0.5 s or more after that measurement had been
received at least once.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Wind estimate jumps
STATEMENT: >>>
The EKF check shall raise a warning when the horizontal wind speed estimate in `estimator_status` changes by
more than 5.0 m/s between two consecutive armed samples.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EKF score and what the result carries
STATEMENT: >>>
The EKF module score shall be 100 less a penalty per finding, with the penalties of each group of findings
capped (innovation flags 60, each solution-flag source 45, filter faults 45, timeouts 30, test ratios 30, wind
10), not below 0. Every finding shall carry the category `ekf`, a `kind`, a confidence from 0 to 1 with its
level, a time window and chart data. The result shall carry the highest test ratio as a key metric when a ratio
was logged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests check that a clean log scores 100, that a finding lowers the score, the confidence range and the chart
lengths. The caps are checked by inspection of `EKFAnalyser.analyse`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EKF advice by sensor and autopilot
STATEMENT: >>>
An EKF finding tied to a sensor (GPS, height, magnetometer, airspeed, range finder, optical flow) shall
recommend checking that sensor. The advice shall name a parameter only where the code holds one for that
autopilot: `EKF2_GPS_DELAY` for GPS findings on PX4, none otherwise. The EKF check shall make no numeric
parameter recommendation.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Ascent profile

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Ascent profile scope and not assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
The ascent-profile check shall take `vehicle_gps_position` (altitude in mm) and shall assess a log only when its
altitude trace has exactly one dominant peak and either the peak is 300 m or more above the first valid GPS
altitude or a boost above 2.5 g lasting 0.2 s or more is found before the peak. In every other case (no altitude
or timestamp column, fewer than 10 samples with a 3D fix, no single peak, a low peak with no boost) it shall
return a not-assessed result with the reason.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Apogee and boost
STATEMENT: >>>
For an assessed log the ascent-profile check shall report the apogee height above the first valid GPS altitude
and the time to it, and where `sensor_accel` shows a boost its peak in g and its duration, as findings of
severity good with their time and as key metrics. Where `vehicle_angular_velocity` covers the boost it shall
raise a warning when the coefficient of variation of the angular-rate magnitude during the boost is above 0.6.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parachute deployment
STATEMENT: >>>
The ascent-profile check shall report a parachute deployment where the descent rate falls by a factor of 2.5 or
more within 3.0 s and stays at 1.0 m/s or more afterwards, with its height and time after apogee; shall raise a
warning when that height is below 10 % of the apogee height; and shall raise a critical finding when no
deployment is found and the log ends at or below 10 % of the apogee height. It shall make no such claim when the
log ends higher.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Ascent profile is not scored
STATEMENT: >>>
The ascent-profile check shall have a weight of 0 in the overall score and shall not compute a module score: its
result carries the default score of 100 whatever its findings.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for an unscored check. The module applies to few flights and the code keeps it out of
the weighted mean of SYS-011 so that it neither dilutes nor is diluted by the other checks.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test reads the weight or the score of this module. Inspection checks that `AscentProfileAnalyser` sets no
`weight` (the base class default is 0.0) and passes no `health_score` to `AnalyserResult`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: All four checks

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DYN-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fixed rules only
STATEMENT: >>>
The four checks shall compute their findings, severities, scores, key metrics and recommendations from the log
data, the parameter set and constants held in the code only, with no random number, no clock and no dependence
on set ordering.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test in the four assigned test files runs a check twice and compares. Inspection checks that the modules
import no `random`, `time` or `datetime`, call no random generator and iterate only lists, dicts in insertion
order and sorted keys. The `id` of a `Finding` is random; it is set by the model in `models/findings.py`, outside
this item.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[[/SECTION]]
